|~ `::bind`, the step that declares a name, and the refusals of a
   declaration. ~|

:BindPayloadNotSchemaError
  |~~ A `::bind` is a map of `:name`, a keyword or a tag, `:docs`, a
      vector of docs, and `:body`, a step.
      ::link~(::bind | doc)

      ~(
        ::bind{:name :inc :docs [1]}
        !| [type /field]
        |  eq [::bind/BindPayloadNotSchemaError :docs]
       )
  ~~|
  ::spec~()

:BindReadBackDiffersError
  |~~ The ::bind prints as text that reads back as another step: a
      declaration binds a body or docs, and a body that is a keyword
      or a tag is written as a group.
      ::link~(::bind | doc)

      ~(
        ::bind{:name :inc}
        !| [type /printed]
        |  eq [::bind/BindReadBackDiffersError ":inc"]
       )
  ~~|
  ::spec~()

:EffectLaunderingAtBindStepParseError
  |~~ A verb whose body calls a name marked `@` reaches outside the
      language, and its own name carries the mark, `:@fetchAll
      ::verb~(@fetch …)`, so every reader of the name sees it.
      ::link~(::bind | doc)

      ~(
        1 | (:bad ::verb~(@callers) | bad)
        !| [type /bindingName /effectfulName]
        |  eq [::bind/EffectLaunderingAtBindStepParseError
                :bad :@callers]
       )
  ~~|
  ::spec~()

:BindNameDeclaredTwiceError
  |~~ A name is declared once in a scope: the steps of a pipeline
      that the pipe or the fail track joins share one env, and a
      declaration of a name one of them declared before is refused
      where it stands. A group, an element, a modifier, a quote and
      a step joined by `*` open scopes of their own, where a name
      of the scope around them is shadowed.
      ::link~(::bind | doc)

      ~(
        :k 1 | :k 2
        !| [type /name]
        |  eq [::bind/BindNameDeclaredTwiceError :k]
       )
      ~(:k 1 | (:k 2 | k) | eq 2)
  ~~|
  ::spec~()
